WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:04.580
One chat request, traced through llama.cpp.

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.830
An HTTP worker thread catches the POST
and routes it to the chat handler.

3
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:14.560
The model's own chat template turns
your messages into a single prompt,

4
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.550
and the tokenizer cuts it into token IDs.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.400
Posted as a task, it gets a slot.

6
00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:23.590
Ideally, one that already holds
this conversation.

7
00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:26.900
Each tick, every busy slot shares one batch,

8
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:29.720
and the KV cache makes room for new tokens.

9
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:34.400
libllama builds the graph: 32 layers
of attention and feed-forward.

10
00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:38.000
Then GGML runs it on the GPU.

11
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.200
Out comes a score for every token
in the vocabulary.

12
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.590
The sampler narrows the field,
and draws one.

13
00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.950
It streams back as a server-sent event.

14
00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:50.280
Then the loop runs again:
one token per tick.

15
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:51.950
Until the model says stop.

16
00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:56.770
The slot goes idle, but keeps its cache,
so your next message starts warm.
